    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28904" root="عرى" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَعْرَى</span></b> ; and its pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَعَارِى</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العُرْيَة</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[The pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعَارٍ</span> [with the article <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَعَارِى</span>] signifies
also (assumed tropical:)  <i>Places that do not give growth to plants,</i> or
<i>herbage.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And (assumed tropical:)  <i>Beds,</i> or <i>the like;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرُشٌ</span>, (K, TA,) pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِرَاشٌ</span>. (TA.) And in this
sense, (TA,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعَارِى</span> occurs for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعَارٍ</span>, by poetic
license. (S, TA.)

